    "body": "I rarely write long reviews, but after 26 days of using the Activated Charcoal Face Wash in Udaipur, I wanted to share a quick breakdown for anyone on the fence. Most botanical products I tried earlier either smelled like artificial perfume or left a weird film behind.\n\nThis formulation is completely different—the texture is smooth and gentle on active breakouts, and over the past 3 weeks it lifts forehead oil and tiny bumps after a long commute without stripping moisture. My skin and hair feel noticeably calmer even on hectic commute days across Udaipur, and a little product goes a long way.",
    "comment": "I rarely write long reviews, but after 26 days of using the Activated Charcoal Face Wash in Udaipur, I wanted to share a quick breakdown for anyone on the fence. Most botanical products I tried earlier either smelled like artificial perfume or left a weird film behind.\n\nThis formulation is completely different—the texture is smooth and gentle on active breakouts, and over the past 3 weeks it lifts forehead oil and tiny bumps after a long commute without stripping moisture. My skin and hair feel noticeably calmer even on hectic commute days across Udaipur, and a little product goes a long way.",
