    "rating": 5,
    "title": "Why I stuck with the Kalpvriksh Satva 7-Tulsi Drops for 2 weeks here in Edappally",
    "body": "Living in Edappally, dealing with the mix of outdoor dust, humidity, and hard water made it tough to find a daily product that cleans properly without wrecking my barrier. I picked up the Kalpvriksh Satva 7-Tulsi Drops 2 weeks ago after reading how they disclose exact active percentages right on the bottle.\n\nFrom the first week of daily use, I noticed that it just 3 to 4 drops in warm water every morning completely settled my seasonal throat irritation, while the glass dropper makes it super easy to carry in my work bag too. Even better, tastes genuinely herbal and potent—one 30ml glass dropper bottle lasts our family over a month. Warning: it's actually concentrated, so don't pour 10 drops like regular market tulsi water!\n\nEverything arrived securely packed in Edappally with a verifiable batch code. What is the best age for kids to take 1-2 diluted drops in water?",
    "comment": "Living in Edappally, dealing with the mix of outdoor dust, humidity, and hard water made it tough to find a daily product that cleans properly without wrecking my barrier. I picked up the Kalpvriksh Satva 7-Tulsi Drops 2 weeks ago after reading how they disclose exact active percentages right on the bottle.\n\nFrom the first week of daily use, I noticed that it just 3 to 4 drops in warm water every morning completely settled my seasonal throat irritation, while the glass dropper makes it super easy to carry in my work bag too. Even better, tastes genuinely herbal and potent—one 30ml glass dropper bottle lasts our family over a month. Warning: it's actually concentrated, so don't pour 10 drops like regular market tulsi water!\n\nEverything arrived securely packed in Edappally with a verifiable batch code. What is the best age for kids to take 1-2 diluted drops in water?",
