    "rating": 5,
    "title": "Why I stuck with the Royal Botanical 2-in-1 Shampoo for 8 weeks here in Amritsar",
    "body": "Living in Amritsar, dealing with the mix of outdoor dust, humidity, and hard water made it tough to find a daily product that cleans properly without wrecking my barrier. I picked up the Royal Botanical 2-in-1 Shampoo 8 weeks ago after reading how they disclose exact active percentages right on the bottle.\n\nFrom the first week of daily use, I noticed that it saves so much time on busy weekday mornings since I can skip conditioning, while it doesn't strip natural oils from the lengths like sulfate shampoos do. Even better, kept my scalp fresh for three full days even with daily helmet commutes. Hard water here usually turns my hair into a broom—this actually made it behave.\n\nEverything arrived securely packed in Amritsar with a verifiable batch code. Any plans for a 500ml family pump bottle? We go through this pretty quick at home.",
    "comment": "Living in Amritsar, dealing with the mix of outdoor dust, humidity, and hard water made it tough to find a daily product that cleans properly without wrecking my barrier. I picked up the Royal Botanical 2-in-1 Shampoo 8 weeks ago after reading how they disclose exact active percentages right on the bottle.\n\nFrom the first week of daily use, I noticed that it saves so much time on busy weekday mornings since I can skip conditioning, while it doesn't strip natural oils from the lengths like sulfate shampoos do. Even better, kept my scalp fresh for three full days even with daily helmet commutes. Hard water here usually turns my hair into a broom—this actually made it behave.\n\nEverything arrived securely packed in Amritsar with a verifiable batch code. Any plans for a 500ml family pump bottle? We go through this pretty quick at home.",
